Dear Anil,

Upon review of HIS-2013-0402 regarding the UT thickness survey for the ATU-100, we have identified that the ultrasonic data for lines 3-RF-101 and 2-RF-102 is not reproducible. The inspection team utilized a carbon-steel velocity setting for these A312 TP316 stainless steel lines, rendering the current thickness measurements invalid.

Consequently, the Hamilton Inspection Department has issued QSCP-NCR-2013-019 to document this nonconformance. All data for these specific reflux lines is rejected, and a full re-measurement at the correct stainless-steel velocity is required immediately to ensure compliance with site retirement thickness and remaining life calculations.

Regards,  Douglas Ferreira Inspection Supervisor QSCP Hamilton Inspection Department  CC: Anil Rao, Halward Inspection Services Ltd.

